    "questionCode": "MH-9-MTH2-1-1.3.1-OSC-101",
    "text": "What is the union of point \\(A\\), point \\(B\\), and all points between \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) called?",
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "Ray \\(AB\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Line \\(AB\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Plane \\(AB\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Segment \\(AB\\) (\\(\\text{seg } AB\\))",
        "isCorrect": true
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "Step 1: By geometric definition, the set containing endpoints \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) and all points between \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) is a line segment.\nStep 2: It is denoted by \\(\\text{seg } AB\\) or \\(\\text{seg } BA\\).\nStep 3: Hence, it is Segment \\(AB\\).",
