    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "solution": "Step 1: In the indirect proof of the interior angles theorem, we assume lines \\(l\\) and \\(m\\) are not parallel, so they intersect at a point \\(P\\).\nStep 2: Then triangle \\(\\triangle ABP\\) is formed with angle sum \\(180^\\circ + \\angle P > 180^\\circ\\).\nStep 3: This contradicts the triangle angle sum theorem (sum = 180°), proving the lines must be parallel.",
